# android/app/build.gradle (signingConfigs section)

```gradle
android {
    signingConfigs {
        release {
            // Keys are loaded from environment variables or a local
            // properties file that is git-ignored. No key material
            // lives in this repository or in the APK source tree.
            def keystorePath = System.getenv("ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH")
                    ?: (project.hasProperty("RELEASE_KEYSTORE_PATH")
                        ? project.property("RELEASE_KEYSTORE_PATH") : null)
            def keystorePassword = System.getenv("ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD")
                    ?: (project.hasProperty("RELEASE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD")
                        ? project.property("RELEASE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD") : null)
            def keyAlias = System.getenv("ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS")
                    ?: (project.hasProperty("RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS")
                        ? project.property("RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS") : null)
            def keyPassword = System.getenv("ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD")
                    ?: (project.hasProperty("RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD")
                        ? project.property("RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD") : null)

            if (keystorePath == null || keystorePassword == null
                    || keyAlias == null || keyPassword == null) {
                throw new GradleException(
                    "Release signing configuration is missing. " +
                    "Set ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH, ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, " +
                    "ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS, and ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD environment " +
                    "variables (or Gradle properties) in CI. " +
                    "Never commit keystore files or passwords to the repository."
                )
            }

            storeFile file(keystorePath)
            storePassword keystorePassword
            keyAlias keyAlias
            keyPassword keyPassword

            // Enforce modern, non-deprecated signing scheme.
            enableV1Signing false
            enableV2Signing true
            enableV3Signing true
            enableV4Signing true
        }
    }

    buildTypes {
        release {
            signingConfig signingConfigs.release
            minifyEnabled true
            shrinkResources true
            proguardFiles getDefaultProguardFile("proguard-android-optimize.txt"),
                    "proguard-rules.pro"
        }
    }
}
```

**Security decisions stated for the operator:**

- Signing credentials are sourced exclusively from CI environment variables or local Gradle properties outside the repository; no keystore file, password, or alias is committed.
- The build fails loudly if any signing credential is missing, preventing an unsigned or mis-signed release artifact.
- V1 (JAR) signing is disabled; only v2/v3/v4 APK Signature Scheme blocks are emitted, which are required for modern Android and resist legacy signature-stripping attacks.
- The `release` build type is wired to the secure signing config and enables minification/shrinking as required by the project rules.
